diff --git a/specter-evaluation/README.md b/specter-evaluation/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e199c5e036fb4efc292d886d0df000e50fc4bbe7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specter-evaluation/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,180 @@
+# Karakeep Brownfield Evaluation Preparation
+
+This directory is coordinator-owned preparation for the frozen
+`lists.addToList` evaluation. The frozen Specter core and verifier are installed
+only as local development inputs; no adapter or domain migration is implemented
+and the production operation is unchanged. The scored adopter owns those
+changes.
+
+## Fixed runtime
+
+- Parent revision: `bc50630767079b060488d1d790b96de1e06ea6ba`
+- Node: `24.14.0` from the bundled Codex runtime
+- pnpm: `11.2.1`, matching `package.json`
+- Web: `127.0.0.1:41736`
+- Rule Engine worker health: `127.0.0.1:41737`
+
+Coordinator preflight on 2026-07-18 completed every check below except the web
+health request: fixed port `41736` was already owned by an unrelated worklog
+process whose working directory was `/private/tmp/specter-worklog-core/apps/worklog`.
+Per repository policy, the coordinator neither stopped that process nor chose a
+replacement port. Re-run the web smoke only after the external conflict clears.
+
+Use the bundled Node runtime and the prewarmed npm cache in each terminal. The
+`pnpm11` function resolves the pinned package through npm's offline cache; it
+does not depend on npm's internal `_npx` hash directory and does not use the
+network.
+
+```sh
+NODE24=/Users/devagr/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin/node
+KARAKEEP_NPM_CACHE=/private/tmp/karakeep-npm-cache
+KARAKEEP_PNPM_STORE=/Users/devagr/Library/pnpm/store/v11
+export PATH="$(dirname "$NODE24"):/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"
+pnpm11() {
+  npm_config_cache="$KARAKEEP_NPM_CACHE" \
+    pnpm_config_store_dir="$KARAKEEP_PNPM_STORE" \
+    npm exec --offline --yes --package=pnpm@11.2.1 -- pnpm "$@"
+}
+node --version
+pnpm11 --version
+```
+
+`NO_COLOR=false` is explicit because some coordinator environments export the
+unsupported value `NO_COLOR=1`.
+
+## Frozen scored inputs
+
+`specter-assignment.json` records the immutable package and snapshot digests,
+the exact preparation revision, the selected operation, and every scored
+command. The committed package archives are under
+`specter-evaluation/frozen-kit/`; pnpm's override forces the verifier's core
+dependency to resolve to that local archive.
+
+The frozen guidance archive SHA-256 is
+`86a847d5dbc0d63089f90f4d4e6fb0283bb4714d89441358b1141b895c0c18d1`.
+
+The coordinator extracted `guidance.tar.gz` before the active-work clock. Its
+contents are available in the ignored, uncommitted
+`specter-evaluation/guidance/` directory. Do not edit the committed archives or
+replace them from the network.
+
+## Clean setup
+
+Begin without a `data/` directory. The seed command intentionally refuses to
+overwrite one.
+
+```sh
+pnpm11 install --offline --frozen-lockfile
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 seed:apply
+NO_COLOR=false DATA_DIR="$PWD/data" pnpm11 db:migrate
+shasum -a 256 snapshots/seed-data-2026-05-20-163735.tar.gz
+```
+
+The required digest is recorded in `legacy-snapshot.json`. Verify the selected
+rows without changing them:
+
+```sh
+sqlite3 -readonly data/db.db < specter-evaluation/verify-snapshot.sql
+```
+
+## Focused validation
+
+```sh
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/trpc exec vitest run \
+  routers/lists.test.ts -t "add and remove from list"
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/trpc exec vitest run \
+  routers/sharedLists.test.ts \
+  -t "should allow editor to add their own bookmark to shared list via addToList|should not allow viewer to add their own bookmark to shared list via addToList"
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 exec vitest run \
+  --config specter-evaluation/vitest.config.ts
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/api typecheck
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/trpc typecheck
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/shared-server typecheck
+NO_COLOR=false pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/workers typecheck
+NO_COLOR=false \
+  NEXT_FONT_GOOGLE_MOCKED_RESPONSES="$PWD/specter-evaluation/next-font-mock.cjs" \
+  pnpm11 --filter @karakeep/web exec next build --webpack
+```
+
+The production build uses Next's supported webpack path because Turbopack
+does not complete in the coordinator sandbox. The committed Google Fonts mock
+keeps the existing `next/font` integration offline; it is build input only and
+does not alter production source or runtime behavior.
+
+The seed archive intentionally contains nine `searching_indexing` queue rows:
+eight pending and one running. They are fixed legacy snapshot state, not leaked
+evaluation work, and the Rule Engine-only worker does not consume them. The
+snapshot SQL verifies those counts, the running job's idempotency key, and that
+the verifier-owned Rule Engine key is absent before the probe. Preserve these
+unrelated rows throughout setup and cleanup.
+
+## Fixed-port web and durable queue smoke
+
+Use `/private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime` for coordinator logs and
+PID files. Start the web server:
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime
+NO_COLOR=false DATA_DIR="$PWD/data" PORT=41736 \
+  API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:41736 \
+  NEXTAUTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:41736 \
+  NEXTAUTH_SECRET=specter-brownfield-local-only \
+  PROMETHEUS_AUTH_TOKEN=specter-brownfield \
+  pnpm11 web \
+  > /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/web.log 2>&1 &
+echo $! > /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/web.pid
+curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:41736/api/health
+```
+
+Enqueue in one process and assert the SQLite-backed pending job from a fresh
+process before starting the worker:
+
+```sh
+NO_COLOR=false DATA_DIR="$PWD/data" "$NODE24" --import tsx \
+  specter-evaluation/queue-probe.ts enqueue
+NO_COLOR=false DATA_DIR="$PWD/data" "$NODE24" --import tsx \
+  specter-evaluation/queue-probe.ts assert-pending
+```
+
+Start only the Rule Engine worker, then wait for the missing-bookmark probe to
+be consumed locally without any external service:
+
+```sh
+NO_COLOR=false DATA_DIR="$PWD/data" WORKERS_HOST=127.0.0.1 \
+  WORKERS_PORT=41737 WORKERS_ENABLED_WORKERS=ruleEngine \
+  API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:41736 \
+  NEXTAUTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:41736 \
+  NEXTAUTH_SECRET=specter-brownfield-local-only \
+  PROMETHEUS_AUTH_TOKEN=specter-brownfield \
+  pnpm11 workers \
+  > /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/worker.log 2>&1 &
+echo $! > /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/worker.pid
+curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:41737/health
+NO_COLOR=false DATA_DIR="$PWD/data" "$NODE24" --import tsx \
+  specter-evaluation/queue-probe.ts wait-drained
+```
+
+## Cleanup
+
+Stop exactly the recorded processes and remove only the verifier-owned queue
+record and temporary runtime files:
+
+```sh
+kill "$(cat /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/worker.pid)"
+kill "$(cat /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/web.pid)"
+sqlite3 data/queue.db \
+  "delete from tasks where queue='rule_engine_queue' and idempotencyKey='specter-evaluation-rule-engine-restart';"
+rm -f /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/worker.pid \
+  /private/tmp/karakeep-specter-evaluation-runtime/web.pid
+```
+
+Confirm the Karakeep worker is stopped, inspect the fixed web-port owner, and
+verify that the verifier-owned task is absent:
+
+```sh
+lsof -nP -iTCP:41736 -sTCP:LISTEN
+lsof -nP -iTCP:41737 -sTCP:LISTEN
+sqlite3 -readonly data/queue.db \
+  "select queue, status, count(*) from tasks group by queue, status order by queue, status;
+   select count(*) from tasks where queue='rule_engine_queue' and idempotencyKey='specter-evaluation-rule-engine-restart';"
+```
